---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SECTIONS } from "../data/sections";

const title = "How Much Does a Life Fitness Treadmill Cost? (2026): Every Model";
const description =
  "Life Fitness home treadmills cost $2,799 to $8,799 on its store on 27 Nov 2026, after up to 20% off: F3 $2,799, T3 $2,974, Run CX $3,919, Club Series+ $6,079.";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "By Price", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/price/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "How Much Does a Life Fitness Treadmill Cost?", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/how-much-does-a-life-fitness-treadmill-cost/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does a Life Fitness treadmill cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On Life Fitness’s store on 27 November 2026 its home treadmills cost $2,799 to $8,799 after a Black Friday discount: F3 from $2,799, T3 from $2,974, Run CX $3,919, Atmos Home Edition from $4,769 and Club Series+ from $6,079. List prices run from $3,499 to $10,999.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is a Life Fitness T3 treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "$2,974 with the Go Console or $3,501 with Track Connect 2.0 on Life Fitness’s store on 27 November 2026, a 15% cut from $3,499 and $4,119. Life Fitness advertised free shipping on the sale.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the Life Fitness Club Series+ treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "$6,079 with the SL console or $8,799 with the 24-inch SE4 touchscreen on 27 November 2026, a 20% cut from $7,599 and $10,999. The console alone accounts for $2,720 of the difference in the sale.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Life Fitness have a Black Friday sale?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes. On 27 November 2026 its store advertised up to 20% off and free shipping sitewide. The F3, Run CX and Club Series+ were 20% off, the T3 15% and the new Atmos 10%; the Symbio Runner and Hammer Strength HD Tread were not discounted.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a Life Fitness treadmill worth the money?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is if you value a gym brand’s frame, a lifetime frame warranty, 10 years on the motor and free white-glove delivery. On features per dollar, Horizon, Sole and NordicTrack give a bigger deck or screen for less, so compare the delivered price and warranty, not just the sticker.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you buy a Life Fitness treadmill on Amazon?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Amazon had listings for the T3 and Run CX on 27 November 2026, but neither showed a price, and an Integrity Series listing showed $2,995, which is low for a club machine. Life Fitness’s own store and its dealers had the clearest prices and warranty terms.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-27",
      dateModified: "2026-11-27",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/how-much-does-a-life-fitness-treadmill-cost/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "price");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const GROUP_PAGES = GROUP?.pages ?? [];
const HERE_AT = GROUP_PAGES.findIndex((p) => p.url === HERE);
// The group's first 2 pages (its leads), then the pages after this one, wrapping round, so every page in a long
// hub group gets sibling links and the leads keep theirs (PLAYBOOK §0b L1).
const MORE = [...new Set([...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, 2), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(HERE_AT + 1), ...GROUP_PAGES.slice(0, Math.max(HERE_AT, 0))])].filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-27",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-27",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "how much does a life fitness treadmill cost",
      "life fitness treadmill price",
      "life fitness t3 price",
      "life fitness f3 price",
      "life fitness run cx price",
      "life fitness club series plus price",
      "life fitness black friday",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See Life Fitness Prices by Model", link: "#price-table" }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/price/">By Price</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Price Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">How Much Does a Life Fitness Treadmill Cost?</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        On Life Fitness’s own store on 27 November 2026 a new home treadmill cost $2,799 for the folding F3, $2,974 for the T3, $3,919 for the Run CX, $4,769 for the new Atmos and $6,079 for the Club Series+, all after a Black Friday cut of 10% to 20% off list. The console you choose adds $496 to $2,720. Here is every model and console priced, what the sale is really worth, what delivery and warranty include, and when a used or remanufactured machine makes more sense.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 27, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">Based on retailer and maker listings, with prices checked on the dates shown.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#price-table" class="btn-ghost">Prices by Model</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        Nothing on this page is a paid placement, and it carries no affiliate links. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Life Fitness is best known for the treadmills in hotel and club gyms, and its home range borrows that reputation:
          heavy frames, long warranties and prices to match. It sells direct through its own online store and through
          specialty dealers, and each model comes with a choice of console that changes the price more than most buyers
          expect. We read every treadmill listing on shop.lifefitness.com on 27 November 2026, Black Friday, including the
          list price and the sale price of each console option, and checked Amazon the same day. Model figures come from
          our own Life Fitness reviews, which are linked throughout; earlier prices are given with their dates.
        </p>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="On this page">
          <h2>On this page</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#price-table">Life Fitness Treadmill Prices by Model and Console</a></li>
            <li><a href="#consoles">What Each Console Costs, and Whether It Is Worth It</a></li>
            <li><a href="#black-friday">The Life Fitness Black Friday Sale: How Much It Is Really Worth</a></li>
            <li><a href="#delivery">Delivery, Installation and Lead Times</a></li>
            <li><a href="#warranty">What the Life Fitness Warranty Covers</a></li>
            <li><a href="#premium-commercial">Premium and Commercial Life Fitness Prices</a></li>
            <li><a href="#used">What a Used or Remanufactured Life Fitness Costs</a></li>
            <li><a href="#vs-rivals">Life Fitness vs Sole, Horizon and NordicTrack at the Same Money</a></li>
            <li><a href="#cheapest">When Is a Life Fitness Treadmill Cheapest?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A new Life Fitness home treadmill cost $2,799 to $8,799 on Life Fitness’s store on 27 November 2026,
            after a Black Friday discount of 10% to 20%; list prices run from $3,499 to $10,999.</strong> Most home buyers
            land between $2,800 and $4,000 for an F3, T3 or Run CX.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>F3 (folding):</strong> $2,799 with the Go Console or $3,295 with Track Connect 2.0, against
            $3,499 and $4,119 list.</li>
            <li><strong>T3 (non-folding):</strong> $2,974 or $3,501, against the same $3,499 and $4,119 list.</li>
            <li><strong>Run CX:</strong> $3,919, against $4,899 list.</li>
            <li><strong>Atmos Home Edition (new):</strong> $4,769 with the SL console or $6,299 with the 16-inch SE4,
            against $5,299 and $6,999.</li>
            <li><strong>Club Series+:</strong> $6,079 with the SL console or $8,799 with the 24-inch SE4, against
            $7,599 and $10,999.</li>
            <li><strong>On top:</strong> the store advertised free shipping on the sale, no membership is required, and
            the Symbio Runner ($21,199) and Hammer Strength HD Tread ($9,467) sit above the home range at full price.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For the brand and how its models differ, see our <a href="/life-fitness/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Life Fitness treadmill guide</a>;
            for prices across every brand, <a href="/how-much-does-a-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how much a treadmill costs</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="price-table" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Life Fitness Treadmill Prices by Model and Console</h2>
<p>
            Life Fitness lists each home treadmill once, with the console as an option on the same page. The table gives
            the “regular” price its store showed on 27 November 2026 and the sale price beside it. Both exclude sales tax.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Model and console</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">List (27 Nov)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Sale (27 Nov)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Saving</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Folds?</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F3, Go Console</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,499</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,799</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$700 (20%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Yes</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F3, Track Connect 2.0</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,119</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,295</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$824 (20%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Yes</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T3, Go Console</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,499</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,974</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$525 (15%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T3, Track Connect 2.0</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,119</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,501</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$618 (15%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Run CX (device-holder console)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,899</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,919</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$980 (20%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Atmos Home Edition, SL</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$5,299</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,769</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$530 (10%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Atmos Home Edition, SE4 16 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$6,999</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$6,299</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$700 (10%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Club Series+, SL</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$7,599</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$6,079</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,520 (20%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Club Series+, SE4 24 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$10,999</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$8,799</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,200 (20%)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Every configuration above was listed as available on 27 November. The Atmos Home Edition carried a “Just
            Released” label; Life Fitness describes it as a 4 HP AC-motor treadmill with a 12 mph top speed and 15%
            incline in a smaller footprint than its club machines. The other figures, from our reviews of each model:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>F3:</strong> 55 by 20-inch belt, 10 mph, 12% incline, 350 lb rating, a 3.0 HP continuous-duty
            motor, folds. See our <a href="/life-fitness-f3-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Life Fitness F3 review</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>T3:</strong> a 60-inch non-folding deck, 12 mph, 15% incline and a 400 lb rating. See our <a href="/life-fitness-t3-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Life Fitness T3 review</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Run CX:</strong> 22 by 60-inch FlexDeck, 3.0 HP continuous motor, 15% incline, 400 lb rating,
            and a console built around your own tablet. See our <a href="/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Run CX review</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Club Series+:</strong> a 4.0 HP continuous AC motor, 12 mph, 15% incline and a 400 lb rating on a
            frame of about 434 lb with its console. See our <a href="/life-fitness-club-series-plus-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Club Series+ review</a>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            On our Run CX review, written earlier in November, the price was about $4,800 to $4,900; on our F3 review on
            21 November, the F3 was already $2,799 with the Go Console. So the F3’s sale price has held for at least a
            week, and the Run CX’s $980 cut is the newest move.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="consoles" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What Each Console Costs, and Whether It Is Worth It</h2>
<p>
            The console is the biggest single choice after the model itself. The frame, motor and deck are the same
            whichever you pick. These are the step-up costs on 27 November 2026.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[600px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Model</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Basic console</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Upgrade</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Extra at list</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Extra on sale</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F3</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Go Console</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Track Connect 2.0</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$620</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$496</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T3</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Go Console</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Track Connect 2.0</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$620</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$527</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Atmos Home Edition</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SL</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SE4 16 in. touchscreen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,700</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,530</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Club Series+</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SL</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SE4 24 in. touchscreen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,400</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,720</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Go Console.</strong> Life Fitness describes it as the console “for a simpler experience”: buttons,
            programmes and a readout, no apps. If you watch a TV or tablet while you walk, it is the console to price
            first, and it is the one that never dates.</li>
            <li><strong>Track Connect 2.0.</strong> Life Fitness says it adds “upgraded connectivity and seamless
            integration with your favorite devices”. It is the middle ground: you still bring your own screen, but your
            sessions can sync. At $496 more on an F3 in the sale, it is about a sixth of the price of the machine.</li>
            <li><strong>SL.</strong> The LED console on the Club Series+ and Atmos. It is the basic option on those
            frames, and on the Club Series+ it saves $2,720 in the sale.</li>
            <li><strong>SE4.</strong> A built-in touchscreen, 16 inches on the Atmos and 24 inches on the Club Series+.
            Life Fitness tags the Club Series+ as <a href="/best-treadmills-for-apple-watch/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Apple Watch</a> compatible. If you want the screen on the machine rather
            than a tablet on a holder, this is the console; it is also where most of the Club Series+’s price sits.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The Run CX has a single console with a dual-zone readout and a built-in device holder, and Life Fitness
            notes that the tablet is not included. Budget for one if you do not already own a tablet you are happy to
            leave on the treadmill.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="black-friday" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Life Fitness Black Friday Sale: How Much It Is Really Worth</h2>
<p>
            Life Fitness’s home page on 27 November 2026 read “SAVE UP TO 20% + FREE SHIPPING SITEWIDE” under a
            “BLACK FRIDAY BEST DEALS” heading, with a slide reading “UP TO 20% OFF Treadmills”. Every home treadmill had a
            lower sale price than its regular price, but the cut was not the same everywhere:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>20% off:</strong> F3, Run CX and Club Series+, on every console.</li>
            <li><strong>15% off:</strong> the T3, on both consoles.</li>
            <li><strong>10% off:</strong> the newly released Atmos Home Edition.</li>
            <li><strong>No discount:</strong> the Symbio Runner ($21,199, with its sale and regular price shown as the
            same figure) and the Hammer Strength HD Tread ($9,467, no regular price shown).</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Is it a real cut? On the evidence we have, mostly yes. The $3,499 and $4,119 list prices for the F3 and T3
            consoles match the figures on our F3 review, and the Run CX price in our earlier review was about $4,800 to
            $4,900, so the regular prices were not raised for the sale. The F3’s $2,799 has been in place since at least
            21 November, so if you saw it last week you have not missed anything.
          </p>
          <p>
            One quirk worth knowing: the T3 costs $175 more than the F3 with the Go Console in this sale, although both
            list at $3,499. The T3 has the longer 60-inch deck, 12 mph and 15% incline against the F3’s 55 inches, 10 mph
            and 12%, so for a runner the T3 is still the better buy. For a walker who needs a treadmill that folds, the F3
            is the cheapest way into Life Fitness this week. Our <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday treadmill deals</a> page covers this year’s offers from
            other brands, and our <a href="/cyber-monday-treadmill-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday treadmill deals</a> page explains
            how the online sales differ.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="delivery" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Delivery, Installation and Lead Times</h2>
<p>
            Life Fitness advertised free shipping sitewide on 27 November 2026, and the store tags its home treadmills
            for white-glove delivery. Our F3 review recorded what that delivery includes, from the F3’s listing on 21
            November: in-home delivery with placement in the room of your choice, <a href="/how-to-assemble-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>professional assembly</a> and packaging
            removal. The same listing gave a lead time of 5 to 7 weeks for delivery and installation, and the T3 and
            Club Series+ listings carried a “2-3 weeks” tag on 27 November.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What it costs</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Life Fitness store (27 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Typical alternative</th></tr></thead>
